From 7387a666ebca7d4a22676c350e4c598ffd831d1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shandongtlb <40312509+shandongtlb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 05:50:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wlan: respect helper self-peer ownership and final PNO
 cleanup

Retuning with Probe traffic reproduced a firmware assert after helper self-peer CREATE_CONF reported EXISTS and the host deleted that peer before STOP. Claim ownership only for a status-zero creation; retain all TX drain and response fences. This fixes the ownership assumption, with firmware root cause and device validation still pending.

Final adapter cleanup has already removed vdev sync when cfg80211 stops its cached scheduled scan. Mark that terminal phase explicitly and acknowledge only its host cleanup, preserving live sync errors. Add extracted-production-code regression tests and record observed device failures. Seven relevant ASan/UBSan tests pass; no full build or new device deployment.
